    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Iron was completely unknown during the Chalcolithic Age; copper was the primary metal utilized.",
        "Ahar (Rajasthan) was anciently known as 'Tambavati' (place having copper) due to local copper smelting.",
        "Daimabad (Jorwe Culture, Maharashtra) is famous for the discovery of four magnificent bronze sculptures, including a chariot pulled by bulls.",
        "Despite being contemporary with the Harappan Bronze Age in some areas, Chalcolithic cultures were rural and lacked writing systems."
      ],
      "id": "nctn03j"
